cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "N = 25A + 12B | The Clock Structure | p ≡ 1 (mod q)"
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: el Issaoui
    given-names: Bilal
    affiliation: Independent Researcher, Amsterdam
year: 2026
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.20273909
url: https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.20273909
repository-code: https://github.com/A19dammer91/the-exact-algebraic-condition-for-clock-behaviour
abstract: >
  This paper analyses the linear Diophantine system N = 25A + 12B,
  where p ≡ 1 (mod q) — the exact algebraic condition for clock behaviour.
  The minimal A-coordinate is directly determined as A₀ = N mod 12,
  without search or iteration. An exact O(1) counting formula R(N) is
  established and compared systematically with the (19,9)-system.
keywords:
  - linear Diophantine equations
  - clock structure
  - minimal representation
  - counting formula
  - p ≡ 1 (mod q)
  - Frobenius boundary
